-- `it.price` is the one real bug: Item (a.wo) has no `price` field,
-- only `n`. Before the hotfix, this body-level WO-E202 check re-ran
-- once per OTHER discovered file too (a.wo's own pass here), so a
-- 2-file program reported it twice -- once correctly at b.wo, once
-- phantom-stamped with a.wo's path at the same (nonexistent) line/col.
fn main() {
  let it = Item{n:1}
  print_int(it.price)
}
